node_modules
dist
*.local
*.log

# Rust build output
src-tauri/target

# Download cache for the pinned Linux device payloads (proot + Ubuntu base
# rootfs) — scripts/build-launcher-apk.mjs refills it, checksum-gated.
.cache/

# Bundled third-party binaries (adb / scrcpy) — restore by unpacking a scrcpy
# release for this platform into src-tauri/resources/bin. Every release bundles
# adb alongside scrcpy, so one download covers both:
#   Windows  scrcpy-win64-v<ver>.zip
#   macOS    scrcpy-macos-aarch64-v<ver>.tar.gz  (Apple Silicon)
#            scrcpy-macos-x86_64-v<ver>.tar.gz   (Intel)
# Flatten the archive's top-level directory — the files go directly in bin/.
# The directory itself is kept tracked via .gitkeep: tauri.conf.json lists
# resources/bin under bundle.resources and the build script hard-fails with
# `resource path "resources\bin" doesn't exist` when it is missing.
src-tauri/resources/bin/*
!src-tauri/resources/bin/.gitkeep
